This sequence mirrors how many senior Java interviews progress: they often begin with Java fundamentals, move into Spring and related technologies, then cover architecture, distributed systems, and coding. Since you've mentioned you feel you've forgotten much of the material, rebuilding the Java fundamentals first will make the Spring ecosystem much easier to revisit.
